      "created_at": "2013-03-16T15:53:29.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>of course. they are environment cards. (what type of card is determined by its Back - if it has an environbment name on its back its an environment card, a villian back a villain card, ect - if it has another picture with more abilities of some kind, its a character card <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>One card defies this though, Kismet's Talisman is double-sided but is not a character card.</p>",
